.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-grid\-file=grdfile \-Igrdfile
Sets a GMT grid file to be read and displayed at startup.
.TP
.B \-\-help \-H
Prints a description of the program and its options, then exits.
.TP
.B \-\-overlay\-file=grdfile \-Jgrdfile
Sets a GMT grid file to be read and displayed as an overlay at startup.
This option has no effect unless \fB\-\-grid\-file\fP also sets a primary grid.
.TP
.B \-\-test \-T
Calculates and displays a test grid at startup, so that the program can be
tried without a grid file.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose \-V
Prints the program version and more information about its work to the
stderr stream. Give it twice for debugging output.

.SH OTHER PROGRAMS
The Action menu items "Open Selected Nav in MBedit", "Open Selected Nav in
MBeditviz" and "Open Selected Nav in MBvelocitytool" start the Qt6 versions
\fBmbedit-qt\fP, \fBmbeditviz-qt\fP and \fBmbvelocitytool-qt\fP with the
swath files of the selected navigation. "Open Selected Nav in MBnavedit"
starts \fBmbnavedit\fP. A program is looked for in the directory
of \fBmbgrdviz-qt\fP, then on the PATH; if a Qt6 version is not found, the
Motif program is started instead.

.SH DIFFERENCES FROM MBGRDVIZ
The realtime display is not implemented in \fBmbgrdviz\fP either: its Start,
Stop, Pause, Resume and Test controls do nothing there. \fBmbgrdviz-qt\fP
disables them. The Realtime Setup window records the navigation source.

The Mouse menu works as the mouse mode buttons: choosing a site, route or
navigation mode switches on that overlay and redraws the map at once. The
Mouse menu of \fBmbgrdviz\fP switches the overlay on without redrawing.

Pressing Full when the map is already drawn at full resolution shows
"Already at full resolution" in the status line.

Messages name the program \fBmbgrdviz-qt\fP; the files it writes say "Output
by Program MBgrdviz", as those of \fBmbgrdviz\fP do.

